<title>UK: UK's Major aims for public spending under 40 pct.</title>
<headline>UK's Major aims for public spending under 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister John Major said his first objective for government spending was to get it public spending below 40 percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>Speaking on BBC radio, Major said, &quot;Our first objective is to get it below 40 percent. We'll get it below 40 percent first and then we will set another target.&quot; &quot;But it's hard to get savings, no-one is pretending it is easy.&quot;</p>
<p>He said Britain's public finances would improve as the economy expanded and government spent money more effectively.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
